What:		/sys/class/accel/accel<idx>/device/ane_stats
Date:		October 2026
KernelVersion:	7.1
Contact:	Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Description:
		Cumulative Apple Neural Engine (ANE) producer counters for
		this device, one ASCII "key value" pair per line, mode
		0444 (readable without root):

		busy_ns: nanoseconds the engine was busy since the
		device was bound. ane serializes submissions
		(M1 family), so this is the sum of the
		submit-to-completion windows; ane_t6021 (M2
		family) can run submissions in parallel, so
		overlapping windows count once.

		jobs: completed submissions since the device was
		bound.

		Neither counter resets while the device is bound.

		The file exists only when the module parameter
		ane.stats / ane_t6021.stats (default 1) is set at
		probe. With stats=0 the driver creates no stats files
		and the submission hot path skips the counters.

Users:		performance samplers that compute engine utilization
		and job rate from the two counters.
